<!--Q#3-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Find three ordered pairs \((x, y)\) that would be solutions to the inequality. Then, explain what that means for Elijah. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
    <para>\((20, 10)\), \((15, 20)\), \((10, 25)\). For each of these coordinate points, if Elijah worked \(x\) hours at the grocery store and \(y\) hours babysitting, he would earn at least $260.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
